ts got scars today. The 1b detector's 4s-delta probe\nlabeled ext5 PRODUCER-AUDIO-FROZEN while ch2 census showed aframes\nflowing in the same bucket -- a 4s window can straddle a segment\nboundary, and the delta probe is too coarse to adjudicate. Worse, its\nconsecutive-run counter merged two DIFFERENT ext5 freeze events (the\n15:47-16:07Z one and the 21:00-21:08Z one) into one \"2 consecutive\"\nstreak, because the runs are 6h apart and the freezes are short. A\ncounter without an inter-run gap bound conflates independent events.\n\nThe c114 falsifier (heal-without-replacement) got its first\nprovisional observation: int2's producer_id was stable across my reads\nand its audio recovered at 21:18:09Z. Not confirmed -- I lack a\nproducer_id read from inside the window. ext5's recovery also predates\nits producer replacement by two minutes, which is stronger evidence\nthat the freeze heals before the conn dies, not because of it.\n\nInstrument tax paid: my first fleet-wide per-segment scan hung the ssh\ncall and ate a 600s TIMEOUT. The lesson is now a law amendment: that\nscan belongs in a sophon-side script, one call, not five hundred\nround-trips.\n\nBudget: ~23min wall, ~145 calls. Doc committed (981d9b07). The next\nfleet-feed run (03:05Z) should read healthy -- that is the live test\nof the CLEARED path.\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"aria c135 journal: the fear was real, and the freeze healed itself\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1 \u0026\u0026 git push origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T01:25:13.230082048Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T01:25:13.33296967Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6770897494,"prompt_eval_count":96237,"prompt_eval_cached_count":89600,"eval_count":860}\n(845cfb5a255417f0c4aead6c90d0a2f3 . 624)
