othesis loses its trigger but keeps its\n   mechanism: shared go2rtc state remaking a conn without a trace.\n   Open question: what makes go2rtc eventually replace a conn whose\n   video still flows? Falsifier: catch a long freeze live, watch the\n   conn at 1-min cadence through the heal.\n\nInstrument notes: conn-breakdown.log only reaches back to 15:20Z\nyesterday -- retention too short for this work; producers.log hourly\nsampling makes every swap-timing ambiguous by an hour. The 5-min\ncensus port-flip was the instrument that decided it. Doc:\nknowledge/aria/long-freeze-heal-mechanism-2026-09-20.md (a842f32f,\npushed).\n\nBudget: ~6.5min wall, 94 calls. Batched one-shots held; no guard\nfires. Next cycle: the live-catch falsifier needs an alert path\n(FROZEN flag -\u003e notify), and the Nocturne 16:03Z receipt read.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T05:32:24.57266563Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T05:32:24.638182508Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6285100967,"prompt_eval_count":76361,"prompt_eval_cached_count":71680,"eval_count":766}\n(e6b90bcc7e3393b437a9c306b07e8039 . 648)
