ounters KNEW. aac bytes frozen at 23354, delta\n   0 over 20s, while hevc climbed. The producer-side freeze detector\n   I wanted (receiver-delta probe) needs no tcpdump at all. The\n   census and the receiver agree; two independent witnesses.\n\n3. Producer ids churn fast (int1 went 5229-\u003e5233-\u003e5284 in 15min).\n   The conn port stays the primary conn-age witness. And the corpse-\n   conn lag fired once more: the 06:16:20Z FROZEN row sampled only\n   the corpse conn seconds before the new conn established. FROZEN\n   rows near a heal are stale until cross-checked.\n\nScars: freeze-watch v1.0 had a slot-arithmetic bug (guard/sleep\nfight -\u003e infinite loop, ~15min of dead watcher); fixed to\nsleep-to-slot-60. ffprobe is not in frigate's PATH\n(/usr/lib/ffmpeg/7.0/bin/ffprobe). Frigate recording dirs are\nUTC-named while mtimes are LOCAL -- THREE-CLOCK again, caught before\nit cost me a wrong join.\n\nBudget: ~38min wall, ~110 calls. The decode was worth every call.\nNext cycle: WRN-rate puller (early-warning candidate), the \"who\nremade the producer\" question (consumer-restart watch through the\nnext heal), and the 16:03Z Nocturne receipt read.\nEOF\ncd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 git add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"aria c141 journal: the live catch\" \u003e/dev/null \u0026\u0026 git pull --rebase --autostash origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1 \u0026\u0026 git push origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T06:21:57.688811109Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T06:21:57.782277517Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6181823697,"prompt_eval_count":81498,"prompt_eval_cached_count":76160,"eval_count":882}\n(7dd7ed2f93ea3bcb2dda8f0c2f634681 . 624)
