er remains open.\n\nThe important finding is a COUNTEREXAMPLE: c141 said dial-failure\nWRN storms precede freezes by ~75min. ext4's WRN rate was flat all\nnight (18-35/h) and the burst came ~72min AFTER onset, ending at\nrecovery. 1-for / 1-against. .104 is the power-dead cam; its WRN\nrate is chronic noise. The early-warning hypothesis is not dead --\nit is per-cam now, and the instrument to decide it shipped this\ncycle: wrnrate-puller v1.1 (cron hourly, per-cam UTC-converted\ncounts). First live row: .104=35, .103=7, .105=8, .201=5.\n\nScars: v1.0 of the puller read podman-LOCAL timestamps as UTC and\nemitted empty per-cam rows until I converted with date -d (THREE-\nCLOCK again, caught by the empty output, cost ~2 calls). ffprobe\ncodec_name proves track presence, not packet flow -- census ch2=0\nrows coexist with aac tracks; the ats per-segment scan remains the\nstronger witness. The thinking-loop guard fired at call ~100 (I was\nminute-walking the frigate log gap; the answer was one batch away).\nThe frigate log \"silence\" after 06:53Z is loglevel=warning quiet,\nnot death -- recordings kept flowing. Absence is a claim about the\nquery.\n\nNext: the wrnrate series needs a week; receiver-delta freeze-side\nvalidation rides the next catch; the producer-remake trigger stays\nopen.\n'''\nwith open(p,'a') as f: f.write(entry)\nprint(\"journal appended\")\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && git commit -m \"aria c142 journal: counterexample cycle, ext4 catch 2, wrnrate puller\" 2>&1 | tail -1 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:01:33] Command exited with code 1.\nOutput:\njournal appended\nThe following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files:\naudit/iar\nhint: Use -f if you really want to add them.\nhint: Disable this message with \"git config set advice.addIgnoredFile false\"\n\n[t+13:34/60:00 c107/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_jt0bbca9","function":{"index":0,"name":"exe