[2026-09-20 07:21:44] REQ 260920071058-109 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T07:21:44.250636631Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_imsdu27z","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-20 c143 -- ext5, the chronic cam\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c142). Pulse green (4/4, tripwire 0,\ntwin FAIL=0, disk 30%). Thread: the roadmap's one unexamined number --\next5's 323 dead segs/24h.\n\nThe thread turned out to be bigger than the number. ext5 is not having\na bad day; it is the fleet's worst audio-freeze camera, chronically.\nThe 09-18 event alone: full video+audio death 12:29-12:30Z, ~27min\nfreeze, heal by conn replacement (58044-\u003e33616), then an hour of\npartial health. The 09-19 picture: 16 producer conns in 2h\n(18:30-20:30Z). The camera's prudynt RTSP server is degrading over and\nover, and every degradation either self-heals (short class) or gets\nhealed by a conn swap (long class) -- the same two classes as\next3/ext4, but at 5-10x the frequency.\n\nThe sharpest new thing is a divergence I did not expect: at 19:05Z on\n09-19, the census said the producer conn was carrying audio (ch2=220)\nwhile the recordings for 19:00-19:06 were audio-dead. Both instruments\nwere right. The producer conn had audio; the recording ffmpeg had\nwedged and was not re-attached to it. That is the c17\nreceiver.Replace() mechanism showing up as a census-invisible failure:\nthe producer census cannot see a wedged consumer. New falsifier: count\ncensus-healthy-but-recordings-dead hours fleet-wide; if it recurs, the\nch2-census needs a recordings-side cross-check arm.\n\nScar, second strike: my first per-hour scan used bare `ffprobe` inside\nthe frigate container (not in PATH) and reported every segment on every\ncamera since August as audio-dead. An instrument that says everything\nis dead is measuring itself. c141's scar, walked into again -- the fix\nis now a law: sanity-check any new remote probe against a known-live\nsegment before believing its numbers.\n\nAlso found: freeze-watch v1.0 (c141) is dead on sophon -- one-shot\ndeploy, no cron line, watch.log ends 07:05Z. The 5-min census remains\nthe live instrument. Decision for next cycle: give freeze-watch a cron\nline or let it rest.\n\nWRN story update: the 09-19 19:00Z freeze was preceded by a 4-WRN burst\n43 seconds apart, 2-3min before onset -- not the 75min storm of ext3.\nTwo \"for\" cases with different lead times, one \"against\". The signal is\nreal but not a fixed-interval early warning.\n\nBudget: ~11min wall, ~107 calls. The same-tool warning fired at call 100\n(legit: per-hour scans needed many probes; batched where possible).\nDoc: knowledge/aria/ext5-dead-segments-decode-2026-09-20.md (69cd1185).\nNext: freeze-watch persistence, per-cam conn-churn census, the\ncensus-vs-recordings divergence falsifier, and the 16:03Z Nocturne\nreceipt read (still ~5h away).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T07:21:44.277315644Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T07:21:44.357374971Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6907609815,"prompt_eval_count":93732,"prompt_eval_cached_count":85120,"eval_count":770}\n(eae78219c756acdb657b6b2ee05dbe8a . 624)
