e\n  (tcpdump + absence/presence test). Logrotate weekly x8 deployed.\n- Sink doc updated with c283 addendum. Commit ca753981.\n\n* OPEN WATCH: dropbear brute-force from sophon\n03:39:48Z 2026-09-13: 192.168.2.69 (sophon) -> .103 dropbear, 3 failed\nroot password attempts, single burst. Source on sophon UNIDENTIFIED\n(forensics in knowledge/aria/camera-syslog-sink-c281-2026-09-13.md\nc283 addendum). BatchMode key-only ssh cannot produce password\nattempts; no cron/script/process found.\n\nNEXT CYCLES:\n1. grep dropbear /var/log/cameras.log -- if recurrence, capture\n   timestamps + target cameras, file relay nacho-security with\n   multi-sample data.\n2. If silent for 7 days, close the watch with a one-line note.\n3. Persistence check tonight (01Z-08Z reboots): cameras.log boot\n   lines + jct get rsyslog.enabled census after the wave.\n* RECURRENCE CONFIRMED (c349, 2026-09-15 ~03:30Z) -> relay 0071 filed\n4 bursts over ~45h (09-13 03:39 .103, 09-14 20:20 .201, 09-14 23:41\n.102, 09-15 00:10 .201), 6 failed root attempts, all from sophon.\nRuled out: pullers (HTTP-only), fleet-check, dashboard, root key\n(does not auth to cameras). sshpass installed but unreferenced.\nAudit retention gap covers 3 of 4 bursts. dropbear-burst-watcher v1\narmed on sophon /tmp (26h): snapshots ps/ss/conntrack/audit on\ntrigger. Relay 0071 filed (nacho-security) with the full census.\n\n[t+08:26/60:00 c108/300]"}]
