[2026-09-20 09:05:25] REQ 260920085310-35 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=70 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_4c7l660e","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/probes/rssi-sizes.probe","content":"### RSSI rotation-sanity + freshness via the LOCAL sophon archive.\n### c146 fix for the dropbear-burst class: the OLD pattern sshed each\n### camera (`ssh root@192.168.2.$ip wc -c /var/rssi.log`) with no key\n### and no BatchMode -> 3 password fails per cam per sweep (24/burst).\n### The archive /var/lib/aria-fleet/rssi/*.log is pulled every 15min by\n### rssi-puller.sh; reading it locally is the same information with\n### ZERO camera contact. Run ON sophon (one ssh, BatchMode).\n### Doc: knowledge/aria/dropbear-bursts-rssi-loop-2026-09-20.md\n### Law (0071): camera ssh probes are FORBIDDEN in ad-hoc command\n### templates; camera contact rides the pullers (curl) only.\n### Serves TWO laws: size cap 180K (APPEND-ONLY-ON-FIXED-STORAGE)\n### and max(epoch) freshness (PULL-SUCCESS-IS-NOT-FRESHNESS).\nfor f in /var/lib/aria-fleet/rssi/192.168.2.*.log; do\n  ip=$(basename \"$f\" .log)\n  size=$(wc -c < \"$f\")\n  last=$(tail -1 \"$f\" 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $1}')\n  now=$(date +%s)\n  if [ -z \"$last\" ] || ! [ \"$last\" -eq \"$last\" ] 2>/dev/null; then\n    echo \"$ip size=$size last=NONE STALE\"\n    continue\n  fi\n  age=$(( (now - last) / 60 ))\n  flag=\"\"\n  [ \"$size\" -gt 180000 ] && flag=\"$flag OVER-CAP\"\n  [ \"$age\" -gt 120 ] && flag=\"$flag STALE\"\n  echo \"$ip size=$size last_epoch=$last age_min=$age$flag\"\ndone"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:05:03] Success: File written to '/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/probes/rssi-sizes.probe'\n[t+11:52/60:00 c32/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_n6c1oqqh","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_loca